Chapter: UnitShow
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `show` on a unit type must answer the value, not the machine
 representation of it. `emit-show-builtin` dispatches on the operand
 type, and until 2026-07-28 it dispatched on the WRAPPER: a unit type
 missed the arm its inner type is entitled to and fell to the
 `otherwise` arm, which is `__itoa`. A unit Text printed 1132612 (the
 pointer), a unit Boolean printed 1 (the raw tag), and a unit Real
 printed 4612811918334230528, which is 0x4004000000000000 -- 2.5 as an
 IEEE double, rendered as a decimal integer. Measured on seed
 759D3E0F and again, byte-identically, on 6ED0A257.

 Every row is asked twice, unwrapped and wrapped, and the unwrapped
 answer is the control. A row means nothing on its own: `show` could be
 broken for Text outright and the wrapped row would still differ from
 the value. It is the two columns AGREEING that says the wrapper was
 seen through.

 The Integer rows are why this was cheap to miss and are kept for that
 reason. `otherwise` is the CORRECT destination for a unit Integer, so
 that row was right before the fix and is right after it. A spot check
 that reached for the obvious unit type would have found nothing wrong.

Section: Types

  Name = unit Text
  Flag = unit Boolean
  Dist = unit Real
  Count = unit Integer

Section: Operands

  plain-text : Text
  plain-text = "abcd"

  plain-bool : Boolean
  plain-bool = True

  plain-real : Real
  plain-real = 2.5

  plain-int : Integer
  plain-int = 42

  unit-text : Name
  unit-text = Name "abcd"

  unit-bool : Flag
  unit-bool = Flag True

  unit-real : Dist
  unit-real = Dist 2.5

  unit-int : Count
  unit-int = Count 42

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("text-plain=" & show plain-text)
    print-line-uni ("text-unit =" & show unit-text)
    print-line-uni ("bool-plain=" & show plain-bool)
    print-line-uni ("bool-unit =" & show unit-bool)
    print-line-uni ("real-plain=" & show plain-real)
    print-line-uni ("real-unit =" & show unit-real)
    print-line-uni ("int-plain =" & show plain-int)
    print-line-uni ("int-unit  =" & show unit-int)
  end
